{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962274,"nonce":"uMbaEgJa7/UZgrO6VtYcOFaOtv4=","title":"Real text measurement is only available through blinc_app","message":"Standalone LayoutTree users get EstimatedTextMeasurer: the font-backed\nFontTextMeasurer lives in blinc_app/src/text_measurer.rs, installed by\ninit_text_measurer (321) / init_text_measurer_with_registry (337).\n\nIt needs nothing from blinc_app. Its imports are blinc_layout's GenericFont\nand text_measure types and blinc_text's FontFace, FontRegistry, LayoutOptions,\nLineBreakMode, TextLayoutEngine and global_font_registry. The one blinc_app\nreference, crate::system_font_paths() in load_system_font (68), fills\nself.font, which no measuring code reads (written at 73 and 84 only).\n\nblinc_text is light (ttf-parser, rustybuzz, fontdb, swash, unicode-*, lru;\nno wgpu or winit), and neither of blinc_text and blinc_layout depends on the\nother, so either direction is cycle-free.\n\nProposed: move FontTextMeasurer and the two init functions into\nblinc_layout behind a feature (text-measurer = [\"dep:blinc_text\"]), drop the\ndead load_system_font, and keep blinc_app's public names as re-exports\n(lib.rs:212, 263). Moving it into blinc_text instead would make blinc_text\ndepend on blinc_layout, which is much heavier.\n\nGotcha for any standalone use: get_for_render_with_style only reads the\nfont cache (registry.rs:845-873), FontRegistry::new() does not preload\ngeneric fonts (195) and preload_generic_fonts (237) is never called. In\nblinc_app the renderer fills the cache (blinc_text/src/renderer.rs:863-905).\nWithout a renderer, fonts must be loaded (load_generic_with_style /\nload_font_with_style) before layout, or every measurement silently falls\nback to estimates.","files":null}]}